# THE BRIDE — Blud's death knight. A pale, waifish swordswoman in lace and
# plate who stalks the player and cleaves. Spec:
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-bride-sword-enemy-design.md.
#
# AUTHORED FROM PROSE plus one inspiration photo the owner showed and which is
# NOT committed (a pale slim young woman, long dark centre-parted hair, raw
# red-rimmed eyes, a white lace veil, a white corset, a short tiered ruffle
# skirt, cream thigh boots, chains and iron crosses, plate arms, a longsword
# held two-handed over the shoulder). The photo was read once for the brief
# and put down: no mesh, no plate, so blob:measure / blob:rings exit 2 and no
# number below is measured — each is a design decision with its reason beside
# it, the broodmother's road.
#
# WHO SHE IS. The broodmother's brief, turned from lust to devotion: built to
# be looked at, and WRONG BY THE SECOND LOOK. At arena distance she must read
# as graceful and female — a tall pale figure in white. Every hook below is
# something that only arrives as she closes, and none of them is allowed to
# spoil the first read.
#
# THE LOOK PASS (owner, 2026-09-24). The first build read as "an alien
# mannequin"; then "i kinda like it but its a bit too alien" — so the target
# is THE MIDDLE: a pretty, doll-like young woman first, slightly otherworldly
# second. The beautiful half is a human skull with a real face, a small fine
# nose, full lips, soft cheeks, a modest female bust, an hourglass and
# thighs that taper like a woman's. The otherworldly half is only a TRACE:
# eyes a touch too large and too wide-set, a high smooth forehead on a
# slightly long cranium, porcelain skin, the long neck and long legs.
#
# THE FOUR HOOKS, and the prims that carry each (this pass is FLESH ONLY;
# later tasks lay cloth, kit, sword and face sheet over these):
#   1. WRONG ANATOMY, THE CHEAP VERSION — the SKELETON carries it, not a prim:
#      the hip joint at 1.04 m (57% of her 1.815 m flesh height; a woman is
#      ~50%), slim thighs with a woman's taper (semi 0.068 at the root to
#      0.035 at the knee, 0.052 probed mid-thigh), a wasp waist (probed semi
#      0.087) between flared hips (probed ~0.17 — carried by the THIGH prims,
#      see LEGS) and a modest high bust, and a 0.14 m neck (~20% too long).
#      bride-blob.test.ts pins the proportions. The SWORD FOREARM is 4 cm longer than the off one (`lenR=` on
#      `forearm`): the vambrace hides it at rest, and the swing arcs spend it
#      as a whip-like reach. No second elbow — motion joints are a fixed set.
#   2. THE VEIL HIDES A WRONG FACE — the head prims: a human cranium, a face
#      mass that tapers to a slim jaw and a soft pointed chin, high round
#      cheekbones over soft cheeks, a small upturned nose, full pale-lilac
#      lips, and almond eyes (sclera + dark iris) set IN the head under
#      heavy, half-hooded upper lids and soft brow arcs, inside flat bruised
#      makeup ovals — a sleepy doll. Pretty in its parts. The upper lids and under-eyes are
#      kept clean surfaces: the WRONG half is the baked sheet (Task 2: liner,
#      lashes, running mascara, corpse makeup, sutures from the mouth
#      corners) and the jaw gape (a later task). The eyes do NOT glow — she
#      is a corpse, not a demon.
#   3. STIGMATA / RELIQUARY — the RIB WINDOW: eight thin rib ridges, four each
#      side of a sternum gap, y ~1.17-1.31 BELOW and between the bust (the
#      costal arch), on the chest bone, which the corset
#      bodice (Task 3) is clipped open over. Plus PAINTED wounds — a small
#      cross at the throat and one on each inner thigh, each with a weeping
#      drip line, in a darker, wetter red than any other paint on her.
#   4. FUSED GAUNTLETS — raw-red flesh BULGES where the plate (Task 4) will
#      meet skin: in both elbow creases and two swellings under the right
#      pauldron's rim; and a flesh CUFF on the right hand that grows past the
#      fist along the grip axis — she cannot let go of the sword.
#
# Blue-porcelain skin with a bruise-violet mottle (the palette); raw red
# 8a2a2a only at the seams; the stigmata 4a0e12, wet.
model bride
  # Flesh crown ~1.81; the scalp mass, hair and veil (Task 3) take her to
  # the spec's ~1.85.
  height 1.85
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # THE HIGH PELVIS (hook 1). Root at 0.96 with a short 0.08 bone puts the
  # hip joint — thigh.l.head — at 1.04 m: 0.57 of her 1.815 m flesh height,
  # against ~0.50 for an ordinary woman. That is the ~10% too-long legs, and
  # it is the one proportion that reads from across the arena as "elegant"
  # before it reads as "wrong".
  root pelvis at 0.96 len=0.08

  # Upright and a little proud: the lumbar sways back 2, the chest lifts
  # (pitch -3). She carries herself; the zombie owns the stoop.
  bone spine1 parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=-2 len=0.15
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=-3 len=0.17
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=0  len=0.07
  # THE LONG NECK (hook 1): 0.14 m, ~20% over the ~0.115 a woman of her
  # height carries, pitched 8 forward so the head floats ahead of the
  # shoulders like a swan's — graceful first, stalk-like on the second look.
  bone neck   parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=8  len=0.14
  # Skull tipped back 4 so the face lifts: the chin leads. The face features
  # below hang off this bone at=0.08..0.62 (y 1.59..1.72).
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=-4 len=0.24

  mirror
    # NARROW, SLOPING SHOULDERS: socket at x ~0.15, y ~1.41 — a slight
    # woman's frame (the deltoid's outer surface lands ~0.19). tilt -8 drops
    # the socket below the yoke's top: at tilt 4 the deltoids rose 2 cm over
    # the shoulder line and read as a mannequin's ball joints. (On a `side`
    # bone tilt swings toward +y, so negative is down.) The WAM pauldron
    # (Task 4) widens the right one.
    bone clavicle parent=spine2   side=0.020 dir=side tilt=-8 len=0.13
    # Arms long and thin, hanging out (tilt 11, forearm 6) so there is
    # DAYLIGHT between wrist and hip flare (semi ~0.16): at tilt 8 / 4 the
    # probed flesh ran unbroken from the navel to the forearm at y 1.00.
    # Forward a touch (pitch 2).
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=11 pitch=2 len=0.30
    # THE SWORD FOREARM (hook 1): 0.26 on the off side, 0.30 on the sword
    # side. lenR= is the grammar's asymmetric-pair word (added for her): a
    # mirror block otherwise gives both sides one length, and a bone outside
    # it could neither parent to upperarm.r nor carry arm prims. The right
    # hand hangs 4 cm lower at rest; the vambrace hides where.
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=6 pitch=10 len=0.26 lenR=0.30
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down pitch=8         len=0.08
    # LEGS: 0.49 + 0.48 from the hip joint at 1.04 lands the ankle at ~0.07.
    # Knees drawn in a whisper (tilt -1.5, shins +1.5) — a narrow, poised
    # stance with a daylight gap between slim thighs. Knee a touch
    # FORWARD of the hip-ankle line (thigh pitch 2, shin -1): a first pass
    # with the shin pitched +1 folded the knee 4 mm BEHIND it, which
    # checkStance reads as digitigrade and the lab refuses to load.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down tilt=-1.5 pitch=2 side=0.085 len=0.49
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down tilt=1.5  pitch=-1 len=0.48
    # The foot bone only positions the foot prims (the house pattern).
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd                      len=0.13
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — the hourglass (hook 1). Waist 0.087, ribcage 0.115 (hips: see LEGS),
  # every mass a tapered bar with heavy overlap so it reads as one smooth
  # body, not stacked discs (the schoolgirl lesson).
  # BLENDS ARE ~1.4-2x the first pass on every round union: buildBody
  # halves them (roundBlendScale 0.5), and the first frames read as a
  # jointed wooden mannequin — a knob at every shoulder, a "diaper" of hip
  # under a stick waist, rings at the knees. A straight 2x overshot: the
  # smooth-min's added volume took the probed waist from 0.089 to 0.131
  # and fused the elbows to the hips.
  # ============================================================
  # Pelvis: the bowl the thighs root in. Semi-width 0.126, bottom at
  # y ~0.89 — kept SMALL. The hip flare is NOT here (see LEGS): the first
  # three passes built it as torso blobs and every one read as a light bulb
  # (a "diaper") hung over two sticks, because torso and leg are different
  # clusters and meet with a hard seam, so no blend can carry the outer
  # line from hip into thigh.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.35 r=0.105 wide=1.20 tall=0.90 deep=0.84 blend=0.028
  # WASP WAIST: one tapered bar up spine1 (y 1.04 -> 1.19). Probed semi-
  # width at its narrowest (y 1.13) is the number the spec caps at 0.095;
  # r 0.080/0.074 x 1.20 probed 0.095 — on the cap, not under it — so the
  # bar is pulled in (and the ribcage's root with it): now 0.087. Shallow
  # deep so the belly is flat.
  bar  torso on spine1 from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.072 r2=0.058 wide=1.16 deep=0.80 blend=0.026
  # RIBCAGE: flares from the waist to 0.115 semi at the top of the chest
  # bone (y 1.36). This is the surface the rib ridges lie on. `core`: the
  # structural mass the arms, neck and hips all fuse to.
  bar  torso on chest  from=0.00 to=0.88 r=0.072 r2=0.098 wide=1.17 deep=0.84 blend=0.024 core
  # A MODEST, CLEARLY FEMALE BUST (look pass): two soft forms high on the
  # chest, centres (+-0.063, 1.342, 0.052), r 0.052, blend 0.012 — ~3 cm
  # proud of the
  # ribcage, bottoms at y ~1.30. (r 0.044 read as pectorals once the lab
  # turntable drew her the right way round — lab-main.ts statue fix.) The first pass's r 0.036 mounds set wide
  # read as nothing, and she read as an alien mannequin. The Task 3 bodice
  # sits over these.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.95 offset=(0.063,-0.0100,0.0660) r=0.052 tall=0.95 deep=0.95 blend=0.012 both
  # THE RIB WINDOW (hook 3). Four ribs each side of a 3 cm sternum gap,
  # BELOW and between the bust: sternal ends at y 1.303 / 1.271 / 1.239 /
  # 1.207, each running out to x ~0.075 and dropping 3.0-3.5 cm — the
  # starved costal arch under the breasts, y ~1.17-1.31. (First pass: 1.28-
  # 1.39, which the bust now covers.) Task 3 clips the bodice open over
  # exactly this strip. Every endpoint's z is the PROBED front surface of
  # the chest there (sdBody with the ribs removed, scratch probe) minus
  # ~1.5 mm, so an r 0.0055 ridge stands ~4 mm proud: ribs pressing against
  # skin, not bones laid on it. bend= is the probed surface bulge at each
  # rib's midpoint over its chord. Unpainted: shading carries them.
  # The chest bone's at=0.50 is (0, 1.275, -0.0095); offsets are from there.
  bar  torso on chest from=0.50 to=0.50 offset=(0.016,0.028,0.0755) tip=(0.059,-0.030,-0.0275) bend=(0,0,0.007) r=0.0055 blend=0.004 both
  bar  torso on chest from=0.50 to=0.50 offset=(0.016,-0.004,0.0700) tip=(0.059,-0.032,-0.0250) bend=(0,0,0.005) r=0.0055 blend=0.004 both
  bar  torso on chest from=0.50 to=0.50 offset=(0.016,-0.036,0.0690) tip=(0.059,-0.035,-0.0245) bend=(0,0,0.005) r=0.0055 blend=0.004 both
  bar  torso on chest from=0.50 to=0.50 offset=(0.016,-0.068,0.0690) tip=(0.056,-0.035,-0.0240) bend=(0,0,0.0045) r=0.0055 blend=0.004 both
  # Yoke + shoulder line: thin front-to-back, semi-width 0.135 — a narrow
  # woman's shoulders sloping into the long neck.
  blob torso on spine2 at=0.90 r=0.060 wide=2.35 tall=0.62 deep=0.85 blend=0.034

  # ============================================================
  # HEAD + NECK (hook 2). The face block is a NUB; every feature is a prim
  # (broodmother's road). Skull bone runs (0,1.568,0.005) -> (0,1.808,-0.011);
  # the cranium's front is z ~0.095 at the eye line, ~0.077 at the mouth.
  # Every feature's z below is set against THOSE numbers (a first pass
  # used z 0.020 for the skull root and buried half the face 1.5 cm deep).
  # ============================================================
  # THE NECK: long — elegance is length — and slim at the top (0.034), but
  # flaring to 0.043 at the base so it grows out of the shoulders: at a
  # constant 0.034 it read as a stalk on a mannequin.
  bar  head on neck from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.043 r2=0.034 deep=1.05 blend=0.028
  # HEAD BLENDS ARE SMALL ON PURPOSE. Smooth-min swell ACCUMULATES: where
  # the cranium, the lower-face cone, the jaw angle and a cheekbone are all
  # ~2 cm away, four blends of 0.02-0.03 folded the field 1.9 cm negative
  # (sdBody -0.003 at a point every prim called +0.016), and the head grew
  # a band 0.092 wide at eye level — goggles, with a moustache of shadow
  # under them. The worst offender was CHAMFER: its reach is 4 x blend and
  # buildBody does NOT halve it (only round unions), so the cheekbones'
  # chamfer 0.008 bevelled 3.2 cm of air into flesh. Chamfers here are
  # 0.002-0.003; round head blends 0.010-0.014.
  # THE LOOK PASS (owner, 2026-09-24): the first head was "an alien
  # mannequin" — a tall egg of cranium with the face squeezed into its
  # bottom third, pits for eyes, a beak. Then: "i kinda like it but its a
  # bit too alien" — aim for the MIDDLE. So the head below is a human skull
  # shape with the face taking the lower ~60% of the head's height, and the
  # otherworldly half is kept only as a TRACE: eyes a touch too large and
  # too wide-set, a high smooth forehead on a slightly long cranium,
  # porcelain skin, the long neck. Pretty doll first, slightly wrong second.
  # World targets (y, z at the centreline): crown 1.813, brow 1.724 /
  # z 0.088, eye line 1.699, nose tip 1.662 / 0.100, mouth 1.635 / 0.093,
  # chin 1.581 / 0.085, back of head z -0.101. The cranium sits 5 mm further
  # back than first placed: its lower front rim overhung the eyes as one
  # shelf across the whole forehead; now only the two brow arcs do. Offsets were solved from the
  # skull point at each at= (y 1.568 + 0.2394 at, z 0.005 - 0.01675 at).
  # CRANIUM: a human braincase, centre (0, 1.722, -0.011), semi (0.071,
  # 0.091, 0.090): rounded at the back, narrower at the forehead than the
  # cheeks, tall 0.97 (a touch long — the trace of the alien). The fattest
  # head prim: the frame the Task 2 sheet projects from.
  blob head on skull at=0.64 offset=(0,0.0008,-0.0053) r=0.094 wide=0.755 tall=0.97 deep=0.96 blend=0.010
  # THE FACE MASS: one tapered capsule from the cheeks (1.676, r 0.054 x
  # 1.20 wide, front z 0.081) down to the jaw front (1.605, r 0.030). Its
  # top dome must stay UNDER the brow: rooted at 1.683 / r 0.056 the dome's
  # upper rim stood out of the cranium's sides and, once the lab rendered
  # her facing the right way, read as a shelf straight across the forehead. This is what gives the face its
  # height; it narrows to a slim jaw with no seam across it.
  blob head on skull at=0.45 offset=(0,0,0.0290) tip=(0,-0.0707,0.0235) r=0.054 r2=0.030 wide=1.20 blend=0.012
  # SLIM JAW: the mass behind the face that gives the jaw line its width
  # (semi 0.056), set back so it never reaches the face plane.
  blob head on skull at=0.24 offset=(0,-0.0005,-0.0050) r=0.052 wide=1.08 tall=0.85 blend=0.012
  # CHIN: delicate — pointed but SOFT, a small round mass (front z 0.085,
  # bottom y 1.581), not the first pass's chamfered spike.
  blob head on skull at=0.12 offset=(0,0.0003,0.0650) r=0.017 wide=1.15 tall=0.95 blend=0.008
  # HIGH SMOOTH FOREHEAD: the cranium's own curve, nothing added. A wide
  # brow fill was tried and rendered as a ridge across the forehead (a
  # Klingon brow in the 3/4 view); the upper lid edge must stay a clean
  # surface for the Task 2 sheet's liner and lashes.
  # HIGH CHEEKBONES, round and broad (chamfer read as a mask edge), out
  # toward the temple at (0.053, 1.678) — OUTSIDE and below the eye's outer
  # corner, not under it: the under-eye stays a flat canvas for the sheet's
  # running mascara (owner ask for Task 2)...
  # NARROWED for the hollows (owner, Task 2 review: "deeper cheek hollows"):
  # the face widened sharply at the cheekbones and the flare fought the
  # painted hollow under it. Outer reach 0.053 + 0.016*1.50 = 0.077 ->
  # 0.046 + 0.016*1.10 = 0.0636 (-17%); height and depth unchanged, so the
  # cheekbones stay HIGH, just less winged.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0.046,-0.0097,0.0550) r=0.016 wide=1.10 tall=0.60 deep=0.85 blend=0.010 both
  # ...and SOFT CHEEKS under them: fullness at (0.040, 1.660), r 0.024. At
  # r 0.020 the 3/4 view showed a gaunt valley from eye to jaw — the alien
  # read. The hollow the sheet paints later goes between the two.
  # Pulled in with the cheekbones for the hollows (owner, Task 2 review):
  # outer reach 0.040 + 0.024 = 0.064 -> 0.032 + 0.022 = 0.054 (-16%). Still
  # above r 0.020, the gaunt-valley radius.
  blob head on skull at=0.42 offset=(0.032,-0.0085,0.0520) r=0.022 blend=0.014 both
  # SOCKETS = where the heavy makeup goes: flat bruised ovals (deep 0.60)
  # sat ~0.5 mm off the face round each eye, 3.4 cm wide — a smoky
  # surround, NOT a pit (pits read as bug eyes) and not a bump (at 2.7 mm
  # proud their rims were ridges under the lid). Bruise red-violet 6a2632,
  # a step lighter than the eye so the almond reads inside it (4a1a26 and
  # the eye merged into one black goggle); the Task 2 sheet paints the
  # smoke, liner and lashes over it.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 offset=(0.034,-0.0007,0.0630) r=0.019 wide=1.35 tall=0.85 deep=0.60 blend=0.004 both color=6a2632
  # EYES: almond — a short horizontal capsule, inner corner low, outer
  # corner a hair up (tip) — 3.3 cm long at r 0.0085, ~3 mm proud of the
  # socket. A touch too LARGE and too WIDE-SET (centres x +-0.034, a woman's
  # are ~0.031): the otherworldly trace. Wet, not glowing.
  # The almond is the SCLERA — a dull, faintly bloodshot off-white (d0c4c8):
  # an all-black almond read as a grey alien's eye, the single loudest
  # alien cue in the look-pass frames. The IRIS is a dark ball set in it,
  # r 0.0068 — a touch too big for the eye, the doll's trace.
  # SET BACK 8.5 mm in all (owner, second look pass: "too bulgy in
  # profile") — with the sockets and lids — so the sclera front sits ~0.077,
  # just under the brow arcs and nasal root below, INSIDE the head rather
  # than proud of it.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 offset=(0.026,-0.0012,0.0727) tip=(0.016,0.002,-0.004) r=0.0085 tall=0.90 blend=0.002 both color=d0c4c8 gloss=0.70
  blob head on skull at=0.55 offset=(0.034,-0.0002,0.0745) r=0.0068 blend=0.001 both color=160c0e gloss=0.95
  # HEAVY UPPER LID — the lidded, half-hooded doll look: the almond's own
  # capsule, raised 8.3 mm and ~0.5 mm proud of the sclera, r 0.0080
  # flattened (tall 0.70), so it caps the top ~third of the eye (raised
  # 6.8 mm it hooded half the eye into a slit). Unpainted
  # skin and a small blend: its upper edge is one clean rounded surface for
  # the Task 2 sheet's liner and lashes. The valley between it and the brow
  # ridge below is the crease.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 offset=(0.0255,0.0071,0.0732) tip=(0.0165,0.002,-0.004) r=0.0080 tall=0.70 blend=0.003 both
  # SOFT BROW RIDGE over each eye (probed front z 0.086 at y 1.72, the eye
  # ~3 mm under it at 0.083; at r 0.016 / 6 mm it rendered as a shelf
  # right across the forehead): the cranium
  # alone falls away to z ~0.074 there, which left the eyes proud of the
  # face in profile. Low (tall 0.55) with a small blend — smooth-min swell
  # between it, the nasal root and the cranium first probed 0.099 at the
  # glabella — so it reads as a brow line, not the Klingon ridge a
  # full-width forehead fill made.
  blob head on skull at=0.62 offset=(0.034,0.0046,0.0720) r=0.012 wide=1.35 tall=0.50 blend=0.006 both
  # NASAL ROOT: fills between the eyes at the bridge (probed front z 0.090
  # at y 1.70) so the eyes sit IN sockets either side of it.
  blob head on skull at=0.57 offset=(0,0.0005,0.0720) r=0.010 wide=0.90 blend=0.006
  # SMALL FINE NOSE, slightly upturned, LOW projection (~1.5 cm): a slim
  # round bridge from between the eyes, then a small tip ball set a hair
  # ABOVE the bridge's end so the tip turns up. The first pass's chamfered
  # cone read as a beak.
  blob head on skull at=0.52 offset=(0,0.0015,0.0847) tip=(0,-0.030,0.011) r=0.0048 r2=0.0058 blend=0.004
  blob head on skull at=0.40 offset=(0,-0.0028,0.0957) r=0.0075 wide=1.30 tall=0.85 blend=0.005
  # STIGMATA, THROAT (hook 3): a small cross over the windpipe at y ~1.50
  # (neck at=0.45 is (0, 1.492, -0.006); front surface z ~0.035) and one
  # thin drip weeping down to the notch. The darkest, wettest paint on her:
  # 4a0e12 at gloss 0.85: a 3.2 x 2.0 cm cross of 1.8 mm bars. At 4.4 x
  # 2.8 cm / 2.4 mm the arms and drip merged into one 2.5 cm red teardrop
  # in the 0.5 m close-up: a wound you see, not a mark you find.
  blob head on neck at=0.45 offset=(0,0.016,0.040) tip=(0,-0.032,0.001) r=0.0018 blend=0.001 color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  blob head on neck at=0.45 offset=(-0.010,0.006,0.040) tip=(0.020,0,0) bend=(0,0,0.003) r=0.0018 blend=0.001 color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  blob head on neck at=0.45 offset=(0.001,-0.016,0.040) tip=(0.002,-0.030,0.005) r=0.0016 blend=0.001 color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  # FULL LIPS: a real upper/lower pair, 3.0 / 2.6 cm wide, the upper bent
  # UP at its middle for a soft cupid's bow, the lower fuller (r 0.0058),
  # both ~1 cm proud at the middle (front z ~0.093 against a face of
  # ~0.082). Pale LILAC b4a6bc (b8a2b8 rendered pink after the sRGB lift). Paint goes to the hit's nearest prim
  # (prim-material.wgsl hitBest), and round lips that claims a patch wider
  # than the lips, so the tint stays a step off the skin — pale, not pink.
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(-0.015,0.0002,0.0805) tip=(0.030,0,0) bend=(0,0.0015,0.007) r=0.0045 tall=0.85 blend=0.003 color=b4a6bc gloss=0.50
  bar  head on skull from=0.26 to=0.26 offset=(-0.013,-0.0002,0.0795) tip=(0.026,0,0) bend=(0,-0.0015,0.007) r=0.0058 tall=0.80 blend=0.003 color=b4a6bc gloss=0.50

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS. Under plate from shoulder to fingertip (Task 4), so the flesh is
  # slim and plain — except at the SEAMS (hook 4). Look pass: a softer
  # shoulder (the deltoid ball moved down the arm, blended wider — the cap
  # read boxy) and a touch more arm (0.038 / 0.031), slim, not sticks.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on upperarm at=0.06 r=0.036 blend=0.030 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.04 to=0.97 r=0.038 r2=0.030 blend=0.016 mirror
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.02 to=0.96 r=0.031 r2=0.022 blend=0.014 mirror
  blob arm on hand     at=0.45 r=0.024 wide=0.75 tall=1.20 deep=1.15 blend=0.016 mirror
  # FUSED SEAMS (hook 4), raw red 8a2a2a where the plate will meet skin.
  # ELBOW CREASE: the couter covers the point of the elbow; the forearm is
  # pitched forward, so the crease faces +z, and the flesh swells ~1.7 cm
  # out of that gap. Both arms.
  blob arm on upperarm at=1.00 offset=(0,0.004,0.027) r=0.018 wide=1.05 tall=0.80 blend=0.010 mirror color=8a2a2a gloss=0.55
  # UNDER THE PAULDRON (sword side only): two swellings bulging out below
  # where the pauldron's rim will sit (~upperarm 0.25-0.30, y ~1.35),
  # outboard and front/back. side=r offsets are NOT mirrored: -x is out.
  blob arm on upperarm at=0.30 offset=(-0.030,0,0.012) r=0.020 blend=0.010 side=r color=8a2a2a gloss=0.55
  blob arm on upperarm at=0.24 offset=(-0.022,0,-0.026) r=0.018 blend=0.010 side=r color=8a2a2a gloss=0.55
  # THE CUFF (hook 4): flesh that has grown over the sword hand and on past
  # the fist along the grip axis (the carry's elbow->hand line, carry.ts
  # gunPoseFromArm), tapering to a tendril ~5 cm beyond the hand bone's tail
  # — into the hilt. Fatter than the mitt so it reads OVER the gauntlet
  # (Task 4 sizes the gauntlet under it). A raw ring where it roots at the
  # wrist.
  blob arm on forearm at=0.97 r=0.026 wide=1.10 tall=0.60 blend=0.008 side=r color=8a2a2a gloss=0.55
  blob arm on hand at=0.10 tip=(0,-0.125,0.018) r=0.031 r2=0.016 blend=0.010 side=r

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS. Long and slim with a WOMAN'S taper (look pass): thigh semi 0.068
  # at the root to 0.035 at a slim knee, a long gentle calf, narrow feet.
  # The first pass's 0.055 stick thighs and knee balls read as a mannequin.
  # The cream boots (Task 4) cover them from the thigh down.
  # ============================================================
  # HIP FLARE — on the THIGH, where anatomy puts the widest point of the
  # hips (the greater trochanter is femur): a mass out and a little back of
  # the hip joint, outer surface x ~0.165 at y ~1.00 (probed), flowing in one smooth
  # leg-cluster blend down the outside of the thigh. It swings with the leg,
  # which is right. The bottom of the hourglass (hook 1).
  blob leg on thigh at=0.09 offset=(0.012,0,-0.010) r=0.057 tall=1.30 deep=1.00 blend=0.030 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.04 to=1.00 r=0.068 r2=0.035 deep=1.05 blend=0.020 mirror
  # Bars run to the joint and overlap: stopped short (0.97 / 0.03) with a
  # knee ball between, the knee read as a doll's ring joint.
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.02 to=0.97 r=0.034 r2=0.021 blend=0.010 mirror
  # (RENDERER BUG, not ours to fix here: a long THIN capsule — the drip at
  # r 0.0024 over 10 cm, length/radius ~50, tapered or not — drew dark-red
  # lines straight out into the air either side of the body at its height,
  # 30+ cm long; the CPU field has nothing there and removing the drip
  # removes them. The drip is now 6 cm at r 0.0025, ratio 24, the same
  # range as the throat drip, which never showed it.)
  # STIGMATA, INNER THIGHS (hook 3): a cross on the inner-front of each
  # thigh at y ~0.87 (thigh at=0.34, flesh r ~0.060; the cross sits 50
  # degrees round from the inside toward the front, so it shows between the
  # thighs from the front). At=0.22 it sat in the crotch's merged flesh,
  # buried 3 cm (probed), once the look pass fattened the thigh tops. A drip
  # weeps 6 cm down toward where the
  # stockings (Task 3) will start. Offsets are for .l (+x out); mirror
  # reflects them for .r. The horizontal arm runs along the surface tangent.
  blob leg on thigh at=0.34 offset=(-0.0386,0.016,0.0460) tip=(0,-0.032,0) r=0.0030 blend=0.002 mirror color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  blob leg on thigh at=0.34 offset=(-0.0463,0.005,0.0396) tip=(0.0153,0.0015,0.0129) r=0.0030 blend=0.002 mirror color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  blob leg on thigh at=0.34 offset=(-0.0386,-0.016,0.0460) tip=(0.0011,-0.060,-0.0011) r=0.0025 blend=0.002 mirror color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  # Calf: a long gentle swell at the back (a tapered capsule down the shin,
  # not the first pass's ball — that was a second knob under the knee).
  blob leg on shin  at=0.22 offset=(0,0,-0.010) tip=(0,-0.110,0.004) r=0.036 r2=0.025 deep=1.10 blend=0.016 mirror
  # Foot: one tapered bar, sole at y ~0.01, arch-high heel end.
  bar  leg on foot  from=0.00 to=0.90 offset=(0,-0.036,-0.010) r=0.030 r2=0.021 wide=1.10 tall=0.80 blend=0.018 mirror

# Wound pass: hidden bone. Torso and skull are AUTHORED — partly for the
# budget (auto-derive would grow a bone in every rib ridge, bust mound and
# face feature) and partly because a headshot and a chest shot are the
# shots players take. Limbs auto-derive (ratio 0.38).
bones
  ratio 0.38
  # Cranium: ~1.5-2 cm of flesh on every side of the (0.071, 0.091, 0.090)
  # braincase, same centre.
  blob head on skull at=0.64 offset=(0,0.0008,-0.0053) r=0.076 wide=0.74 tall=0.92 deep=0.90
  # Spine through the waist, a ribcage, a pelvic bowl.
  bar  torso on spine1 from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.024
  blob torso on chest  at=0.55 r=0.062 wide=1.25 tall=1.25 deep=0.85
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.30 r=0.080 wide=1.25 tall=0.80 deep=0.85

# No mesh, so no bake yet: every face feature is a prim above and the face
# block is a NUB so the parameterised ellipsoid cannot fight the cranium.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006

# THE CORPSE MAKEUP (Task 2): a GENERATED sheet (scripts/make-bride-face.py —
# no reference mesh, so blob:face-bake cannot run). Smoky black sockets,
# bruised lids, winged liner, painted lashes, running mascara, grey-lilac
# lips, sutures from the mouth corners, temple veins and SUNKEN CHEEKS as
# paint (owner: the hollow look without touching the geometry).
#
# PROJECTION, solved from the built body (buildBody + headShape): hs is
# normalised by the cranium (the fattest head prim: centre y 1.7223, semi
# 0.07097 x 0.09118). projScale is a FREQUENCY — lower is bigger; 0.40 makes
# one sheet span 2.5 head units (0.177 m across, 0.228 m down), brow to chin
# and cheek to cheek. The painter centres its drawing on hs (0, -0.5),
# mid-face (eyes at hs.y -0.247, mouth at -0.955); uv.y = hs.y*scale +
# centre, and the drawing's centre sits at uv 0.5, so centre = 0.5 +
# 0.5*0.40 = 0.70. The painter's constants MUST match these four numbers.
#
# BLEND: decal 0 (multiply) with blendLuma 0 (rgb multiply, mode 1) — NOT the
# house default blendLuma 1. The luma default exists because a SKIN-TONED
# bake times skin-toned flesh compounds the hue (the "over-saturated face"
# owner note). This sheet's base is a NEUTRAL grey, so rgb multiply adds no
# hue there, and the makeup's hues (bruise red, violet hollow, blue veins,
# lilac lips) are the point — luma would flatten them all to grey. The sheet
# carries a grey base under the makeup on purpose: the shader divides by the
# mean of every covered texel, so ink with nothing around it would be its
# own mean and multiply by ~1 (the painter's header has the arithmetic).
#
# PAINTED prims IGNORE the sheet (paint-char runs after the face pass): the
# sclera, iris, socket ovals and lips keep their color=. So the smoke is
# painted on the skin AROUND them — lid, brow valley, under-eye below hs
# -0.37 — which a banded diagnostic sheet located (NOTES.md, Task 2).
#
# Her eyes do not glow (eyeGlowCut 0.99 / eyeGlowAmp 0 — the sheet's base is
# a bright grey, and an ungated sheet glows wherever it is bright).
sheet
  image       bride-face.png
  decal       0
  blendLuma   0
  projScaleX  0.40
  projScaleY  0.40
  projCentreX 0.50
  projCentreY 0.70
  eyeGlowCut  0.99
  eyeGlowAmp  0
  # Luminance relief at ~a fifth of the 1.4 default: at 1.4, and still at
  # 0.6, every thin ink line (the mascara runs, the sutures) embossed as a
  # groove with a lit rim — the stitches read WHITE in the 3/4. The broad
  # hollows and sockets keep a trace of sink at 0.3.
  texRelief   0.3

# BLUE PORCELAIN: a cold, slightly blue pale (linear 0.62 0.64 0.70) — not
# the schoolgirl's warm skin, not the zombie's grey-green: a body kept too
# long in a cold chapel. A bruise-VIOLET mottle (a hue shift, not a darker
# base, or it vanishes — broodmother). Translucent enough to glow a little at
# the rim, a faint wet sheen: beautiful first.
palette
  baseColor     0.62 0.64 0.70
  deepColor     0.50 0.05 0.08
  charColor     0.07 0.05 0.06
  specIntensity 0.45
  specRoughness 0.38
  fresnelBoost  0.35
  translucency  0.25
  wetness       0.20
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.015
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.004
  mottleAmp     0.30
  mottleScale   2.2
  mottleColor   0.36 0.26 0.42
